The Go rendering: a command executing one template per shape, each parsed from
a constant string. A template in a package-level variable and in two locals
names a field nothing writes; another names one the program writes; an
html/template set is executed by name. Five templates print a value whole:
the argument by {{.}} and printf, a field by {{.Inner}}, each element by range,
the value with binds, and a variable. One template invokes a defined template
on each element. Two actions reach their value through a method result and an
interface field, one through a template function's result, and one execution's
argument is a reflect.Value.

